    ],
    [
     "Objectives The aim of the work package is to enable smooth progress of the research work in ReCoSE with the required quality and schedules. Co-design workshops (2-3) will be organized to support the iterative material and product development between all consortium partners.",
     ""
    ],
    [
     "Task descriptions – WP5 includes 3 tasks: Task 5.1 Administrative management of project execution Drafting, commenting on, organizing signature rounds, and managing changes to the consortium agreement. Organizing project steering group meetings, including preparing agendas, arranging meetings, participating in meetings, documenting minutes, and sharing event materials. Requesting quotations for meeting room bookings when necessary. Participation in project monthly work package (WP) meetings and providing support as needed in their organization. Task 5.2 Co-design activities Organising and facilitating co-design workshops (2-3 workshops during project time) for industrial and academic partners The purpose of the workshops is to gather industrial development challenges and corresponding material and process requirements as a basis for selecting research project demos and prototypes. Additionally, the goal is to collectively assess the results obtained so far and guide the continuation of the research in this regard. This task is supporting especially WP2 and WP3. Task 5.3 Project documentation, reporting and risk management Providing and maintaining processes and related management tools and methods for executing the project and supervising the execution of the project following the practices set for realisation and management of the research project. Building project management tools, including establishing and maintaining a shared workspace, including project documentation management. Monitoring the progress of work packages and managing the project schedule to achieve high quality results. Monitoring and managing project risks. Guidance and coordination of consortium project reporting. Acting as a representative of the consortium towards National Innovation Agency together with the scientific leader of the project. Outcomes: • Project meeting agendas & minutes. Consortium agreement prepared and signed. • Co-design workshops between all consortium members, well-organized project management and web-based portal for facilitating the internal and external information archiving and exchange relating to and within project • Regular updates between National Innovation Agency and the consortium, support in form of templates for reporting the costs and international activities. Partners: All partners will take part in the joint activities. NISM will take the leading role within the research partners’ consortium and NLUAS UAS will lead the management of the consortium. Project coordination services are being tendered. The consortium authorizes one of the partners (NLUAS) to represent the consortium in the tender.",
     ""
    ]
   ],
